SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Democratic Republic of the Congo: Freedom in the World 2022 Country Report","publisher":"Freedom House","publication_date":"2022","url":"https://freedomhouse.org/country/democratic-republic-congo/freedom-world/2022","claim":"Freedom House says opposition parties and civil society viewed Tshisekedi's 2021 CENI reform as an attempt to keep the electoral body under presidential control, and it says the CENI and Constitutional Court lacked independence.","locator":"lines 113-116","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Major annual country report from a well-established monitor, with direct institutional findings and contemporaneous context.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Near-period country assessment covering the 2021-2022 transition into the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributes the CENI reform and control concerns to Tshisekedi's administration.","contrary_evidence":["The same report notes some opposition members were released from prison and some exiled politicians returned."],"lenses":["4B.1","4B.2","4B.4","4B.8"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"2022 Country Report on Human Rights Practices: Democratic Republic of the Congo","publisher":"U.S. Department of State","publication_date":"2023-03-20","url":"https://www.ecoi.net/en/document/2089109.html","claim":"The report says the state of siege in North Kivu and Ituri transferred powers from civilian to military authorities, restricted rights, extended military-court jurisdiction, and suspended immunity for elected officials.","locator":"lines 40-43","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official annual human-rights report with explicit DRC-specific findings and clear period coverage.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly covers the 2022 target period.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributes the state-of-siege framework to Tshisekedi's presidency and its effects to his administration.","contrary_evidence":["The report also says the government took some steps to investigate and punish abuses, though impunity remained widespread."],"lenses":["4B.4","4B.8","4B.9"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"DRC: One year on, 'State of Siege' used as a tool to crush dissent","publisher":"Amnesty International","publication_date":"2022-05-10","url":"https://www.amnesty.org/en/latest/news/2022/05/drc-one-year-on-state-of-siege/","claim":"Amnesty says the state of siege was used to crush dissent, with activists arbitrarily detained, protesters attacked, and critics silenced in North Kivu and Ituri.","locator":"lines 64-70 and 88-101","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous NGO briefing with specific cases, named provinces, and direct attribution of abuses.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Target-year adjacent evidence within the same 2022 governance environment.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributes the restrictive emergency regime to President Tshisekedi and his security authorities.","contrary_evidence":["Amnesty notes the government said the measure was meant to protect civilians and fight armed groups."],"lenses":["4B.3","4B.4","4B.9"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Pre-election tension in DRC fuels attacks on reporters covering politics","publisher":"Reporters Without Borders","publication_date":"2022","url":"https://rsf.org/en/pre-election-tension-drc-fuels-attacks-reporters-covering-politics","claim":"RSF says at least seven journalists were harassed or attacked in Kinshasa and Kananga in July 2022, and it warns that the political climate around Tshisekedi's bid for another term was endangering media work.","locator":"lines 307-312","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Specialized press-freedom monitor with concrete contemporaneous reporting, though the page date is not fully explicit in the excerpt.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in the target year and tied to the pre-election environment.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but relevant: the article ties the climate to Tshisekedi's re-election drive and the authorities' duty to protect media.","contrary_evidence":["The piece frames the issue as a broader political tension, not only a direct order from the presidency."],"lenses":["4B.3","4B.6","4B.8"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Two Congolese journalists detained for 5 months after covering a protest","publisher":"Committee to Protect Journalists","publication_date":"2022-05-17","url":"https://cpj.org/2022/05/two-congolese-journalists-detained-for-5-months-after-covering-a-protest/","claim":"CPJ says Patrick Lola and Christian Bofaya were held for more than five months after covering a protest, and that the arrests were politically motivated.","locator":"lines 515-518","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Specialized press-freedom monitor with named journalists, dates, and direct legal-process details.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but strong: the article links the detentions to protest coverage critical of local authorities in Tshisekedi's DRC.","contrary_evidence":["The arrests were carried out by provincial authorities, so the immediate attribution is local rather than purely presidential."],"lenses":["4B.3","4B.6","4B.9"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Congolese journalists Patrick Lola and Christian Bofaya unable to pay bail, denied release","publisher":"Committee to Protect Journalists","publication_date":"2022-08-24","url":"https://cpj.org/2022/08/congolese-journalists-patrick-lola-and-christian-bofaya-unable-to-pay-bail-denied-release/","claim":"CPJ says the two journalists remained detained because they could not pay bail of 2 million Congolese francs each after being arrested while covering a political protest.","locator":"lines 515-522","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Specialized monitor with precise dates, bail amount, and detention outcome based on court documents and lawyer testimony.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but relevant to ruler responsibility because the detention flowed through the Congolese court and police system under Tshisekedi's administration.","contrary_evidence":["The court formally set bail, so the abuse here is in the scale and consequence of the bail, not the absence of any judicial process."],"lenses":["4B.3","4B.6","4B.9"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Three Congolese radio journalists stripped, beaten by intelligence agents","publisher":"Committee to Protect Journalists","publication_date":"2022-05-25","url":"https://cpj.org/2022/05/three-congolese-radio-journalists-stripped-beaten-by-intelligence-agents/","claim":"CPJ says the head of the National Intelligence Agency in Tshuapa summoned three journalists after a broadcast criticizing alleged surveillance of students, then ordered them stripped and beaten.","locator":"lines 517-518","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Detailed contemporaneous report with named agency officials, journalists, and a specific broadcast trigger.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Directly implicates a state intelligence service operating under the national government.","contrary_evidence":["The abuse was provincial and agency-specific, not a formal national media policy statement."],"lenses":["4B.6","4B.9"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Congolese journalist Dimanche Kamate arrested, detained over broadcast about Rwanda, protests","publisher":"Committee to Protect Journalists","publication_date":"2022-08-17","url":"https://cpj.org/2022/08/congolese-journalist-dimanche-kamate-arrested-detained-over-broadcast-about-rwanda-protests/","claim":"CPJ says national police arrested and detained Dimanche Kamate for several hours after a broadcast that included civil-society commentary on Rwanda and protests.","locator":"lines 516-516","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Specific contemporaneous case with named journalist, police action, and broadcast content.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Directly relevant to state policing and media control under Tshisekedi's government.","contrary_evidence":["The detention was temporary, so it shows intimidation more than long-term imprisonment."],"lenses":["4B.6","4B.9"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"DRC journalist Tatiana Osango sexually assaulted, two other journalists attacked by police in separate incident","publisher":"Committee to Protect Journalists","publication_date":"2022-09-23","url":"https://cpj.org/2022/09/drc-journalist-tatiana-osango-sexually-assaulted-two-other-journalists-attacked-by-police-in-separate-incident/","claim":"CPJ says an opposition politicians' supporters sexually assaulted Tatiana Osango while she was covering a meeting, and police separately beat two other journalists covering a protest in Kinshasa.","locator":"lines 516-522","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Strong contemporaneous reporting with named victims, perpetrators, dates, and supporting local press-freedom references.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in the target year.","ruler_attribution":"The police attack is directly attributable to state actors; the opposition-supporter assault shows a wider hostile political environment the state failed to control.","contrary_evidence":["One assault was by opposition supporters rather than state authorities, so it is not all ruler-attributable."],"lenses":["4B.3","4B.6","4B.9"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Armed men in military uniforms beat, threaten lives of Congolese journalists Parfait Katoto and Picard Luhavo","publisher":"Committee to Protect Journalists","publication_date":"2022-09-16","url":"https://cpj.org/2022/09/armed-men-in-military-uniforms-beat-threaten-lives-of-congolese-journalists-parfait-katoto-and-picard-luhavo/","claim":"CPJ reports that armed men dressed in Congolese military uniforms forcibly entered two journalists' homes in Ituri, beat them, and threatened their lives.","locator":"lines 516-516","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Specific named victims, dates, and modus operandi, with direct local corroboration in the article.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Strongly relevant because the attackers wore military-style uniforms in a province under national security control.","contrary_evidence":["The article does not prove the attackers were official soldiers, only that they wore uniforms resembling them."],"lenses":["4B.6","4B.9"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Armed men in military uniforms raid Congolese broadcaster, beat technician, and seize equipment, forcing radio station off air","publisher":"Committee to Protect Journalists","publication_date":"2022-09-21","url":"https://cpj.org/2022/09/armed-men-in-military-uniforms-raid-congolese-broadcaster-beat-technician-and-seize-equipment-forcing-radio-station-off-air/","claim":"CPJ says four armed men in military-style uniforms raided Radio Evanglique Butembo-Oicha, beat a technician, seized equipment, and forced the station off air.","locator":"lines 517-517","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous press-freedom report with named station, place, and concrete abuses.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Relevant to state responsibility because the attackers presented themselves as military personnel in a security-sensitive area.","contrary_evidence":["The attackers were not conclusively identified as official army personnel in the article."],"lenses":["4B.6","4B.9"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Congolese journalists face death threats as M23 rebels advance, flee for safety","publisher":"Committee to Protect Journalists","publication_date":"2022-11-03","url":"https://cpj.org/2022/11/congolese-journalists-face-death-threats-as-m23-rebels-advance-flee-for-safety/","claim":"CPJ says at least 23 journalists fled to MONUSCO in late October 2022 after the M23 takeover and threats to kill local journalists.","locator":"lines 515-517","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Strong contemporaneous reporting with a precise count of displaced journalists and a clear threat context.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Mostly indirect, because the immediate threat came from M23 rather than the presidency, but it shows the broader political-freedom environment Tshisekedi governed.","contrary_evidence":["The immediate perpetrators were a rebel group, so the article is more about inherited insecurity than direct presidential repression."],"lenses":["4B.3","4B.6","4B.9","4B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"RDC: Jean Marc Kabund arrete","publisher":"Actualite.cd","publication_date":"2022-08-09","url":"https://actualite.cd/2022/08/09/rdc-jean-marc-kabund-arrete","claim":"Actualite.cd reports that Jean-Marc Kabund was arrested before his parliamentary immunity was lifted and sent to Makala after remarks deemed insulting to the president.","locator":"lines 93-99","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous local reporting with named lawyer, police reference, and direct procedural detail.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Directly relevant because Kabund was a former presidential ally turned opposition figure arrested after attacking Tshisekedi publicly.","contrary_evidence":["The article presents the arrest through the justice process, so it does not by itself prove a presidential order."],"lenses":["4B.3","4B.9"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"RDC: Felix Tshisekedi prend acte du serment de trois nouveaux juges de la Cour constitutionnelle","publisher":"Actualite.cd","publication_date":"2022-06-15","url":"https://actualite.cd/index.php/2022/06/15/rdc-felix-tshisekedi-prend-acte-du-serment-de-trois-nouveaux-juges-de-la-cour","claim":"Actualite.cd reports that Tshisekedi presided over the swearing-in of three new Constitutional Court judges who replaced sitting judges, placing the presidency at the center of court staffing.","locator":"lines 112-118","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Local contemporaneous reporting on a formal judicial appointment ceremony, with direct quotations from the oath.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Tshisekedi's formal role in judicial appointments.","contrary_evidence":["The article does not show whether the appointments were independently selected or politically motivated in practice."],"lenses":["4B.4","4B.5"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Kinshasa : la police disperse la marche des partisans du parti de Kabund","publisher":"Radio Okapi","publication_date":"2022-08-30","url":"https://www.radiookapi.net/2022/08/30/actualite/politique/kinshasa-la-police-disperse-la-marche-des-partisans-du-parti-de","claim":"Radio Okapi says police dispersed a march by supporters of Kabund's party in Kinshasa even though organizers said they had notified authorities in advance.","locator":"lines 152-160","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Local broadcaster with direct reporting on police action, organizer complaint, and the march's stated purpose.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Directly relevant to the government's tolerance of opposition mobilization in Tshisekedi's capital.","contrary_evidence":["Police said the march had not been authorized, so the state gave a legality-based justification."],"lenses":["4B.3","4B.9"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Jean-Marc Kabund: 'Le regime Tshisekedi a lamentablement echoue'","publisher":"Radio Okapi","publication_date":"2022-07-18","url":"https://www.radiookapi.net/2022/07/18/actualite/politique/jean-marc-kabund-le-regime-tshisekedi-lamentablement-echoue","claim":"Radio Okapi quotes Kabund publicly denouncing Tshisekedi's regime as a failure and saying tribalism and regionalism had returned.","locator":"lines 141-150","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct local quotation from a prominent opposition figure in a contemporaneous radio report.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Directly in the target year, but this is opposition speech rather than ruler conduct.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect only: it shows opposition criticism and the broader political atmosphere around Tshisekedi.","contrary_evidence":["This item is a statement by the opposition, not an act by Tshisekedi himself."],"lenses":["4B.3"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Congo arrests opposition leader Kabund","publisher":"The Star / Reuters","publication_date":"2022-08-10","url":"https://www.thestar.com.my/news/world/2022/08/10/congo-arrests-opposition-leader-kabund","claim":"Reuters reports that Jean-Marc Kabund was arrested after falling out with Tshisekedi, and says the episode highlighted emerging fault lines in the ruling coalition.","locator":"lines 131-133","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reporting syndicated by a mainstream outlet, with named actor, date, and clear political context.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Directly relevant to the president's treatment of a former close ally turned opposition leader.","contrary_evidence":["The story does not establish a direct presidential instruction for the arrest."],"lenses":["4B.3","4B.9","4B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Top Congo presidential adviser resigns after allegedly requesting bribe on tape","publisher":"Investing.com / Reuters","publication_date":"2022-09-16","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/world-news/top-congo-presidential-adviser-resigns-after-allegedly-requesting-bribe-on-tape-2894087","claim":"Reuters says a top Tshisekedi adviser resigned after an alleged bribe tape, and the president's office framed the case as evidence that people in the presidency would face consequences for violating the law.","locator":"lines 418-431","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reporting on a concrete corruption case with a presidential response and named adviser.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Directly concerns the president's inner circle and how Tshisekedi handled an integrity scandal.","contrary_evidence":["This is a corruption/accountability case, not direct proof of political liberalization or repression."],"lenses":["4B.2","4B.5","4B.4"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Human Rights Documents - DRC report listing","publisher":"OHCHR","publication_date":"2022-08-10","url":"https://ap.ohchr.org/documents/dpage_f.aspx?c=51&su=60","claim":"OHCHR's DRC document index lists A/HRC/51/61, the 10 August 2022 report on the human rights situation and UNJHRO activities in the DRC, covering 1 June 2021 to 31 May 2022.","locator":"lines 9-10","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"medium","source_confidence_reason":"This is source metadata rather than substantive findings, but it is an official UN index confirming the report's existence and period coverage.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Period-adjacent context, not direct evidence on its own.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect only; it identifies an official UN report relevant to the same governance period.","contrary_evidence":["The listing itself contains no substantive findings."],"lenses":["4B.3","4B.6","4B.9"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Protesters in Congo call for the release of political prisoners","publisher":"Associated Press","publication_date":"2024","url":"https://apnews.com/article/congo-opposition-tshisekedi-protest-political-prisoners-acc468f3ee48045d375294140d560101","claim":"AP says protesters accused Tshisekedi of trying to muzzle opponents and silence dissenting voices while demanding the release of Kabund, Mukebayi, and Kikuni.","locator":"lines 1863-1894","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Major wire report with named protest organizers and direct quotation, but published after the target year.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Post-period confirmation of a continuing repression pattern, not direct 2022 evidence.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but relevant to the longer Tshisekedi trajectory.","contrary_evidence":["This article is outside the 2022 target period, so it should not be used as direct evidence for the target year."],"lenses":["4B.3","4B.9","4B.10"]}

Search ledger: candidates found about 35, documents opened 23, duplicates 4, irrelevant/out-of-period 3, inaccessible 5, accepted distinct URLs 20.

Material gaps:
- Direct 2022 evidence on election-rule manipulation and election-commission capture is still thinner than the press/security evidence.
- Direct 2022 term-limit, succession, and constitutional-transfer evidence is still limited.
- I found weak or no direct 2022 evidence on surveillance, internet shutdowns, or digital controls by the presidency.
- Minority-, women's-, and opposition-region-specific political-equality evidence is thinner than the repression/media evidence.

